{
 "id": "l27",
 "label": "27",
 "title": "Para sa and para kay: for and to",
 "summary": "Spotting the indirect object: para sa and para kay (for), sa and kay (to), and kina for two or more names",
 "minutes": 30,
 "goals": [
  "Know what an indirect object is",
  "Use para sa / sa before a pronoun, and para kay / kay before a person's name",
  "Make sentences with no verb using itó and iyán",
  "Use kina and para kina for two or more names"
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "What is an indirect object?",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "An **indirect object** is a noun or pronoun. In English it answers one of these questions: *to whom?*, *to what?*, *for whom?* or *for what?*. In *He bought a book for me*, the indirect object is *me*."
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "In Tagalog the indirect object is easy to spot, because it is always introduced by one of four prepositions: **[[para kay|marker]]**, **[[para sa|marker]]**, **[[kay|marker]]** and **[[sa|marker]]**."
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "Preposition",
      "Means"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "[[para sa|marker]], [[para kay|marker]]",
       "for"
      ],
      [
       "[[sa|marker]], [[kay|marker]]",
       "to"
      ]
     ],
     "title": "For and to"
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "rule",
     "title": "Sa and kay are not interchangeable",
     "items": [
      "**para sa / sa** + possessive pronoun (+ ligature **-g** + noun, optional)",
      "**para kay / kay** + proper name of a person"
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "pattern",
     "title": "The two formulas",
     "rows": [
      {
       "label": "Pronoun",
       "chips": [
        {
         "t": "para sa",
         "r": "marker"
        },
        {
         "t": "ákin",
         "r": "poss"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "label": "Pronoun + -g + noun",
       "chips": [
        {
         "t": "para sa",
         "r": "marker"
        },
        {
         "t": "áking",
         "r": "poss"
        },
        {
         "t": "iná",
         "r": "noun"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "label": "Name",
       "chips": [
        {
         "t": "para kay",
         "r": "marker"
        },
        {
         "t": "Mary",
         "r": "noun"
        }
       ]
      }
     ],
     "note": "for me / for my mother / for Mary"
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "english",
     "title": "Seen before",
     "t": "You met the same split in Lesson 11: **káysa kay** goes before the name of a person, **káysa sa** before a place or thing."
    }
   ]
  },
