    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "tip",
     "title": "Notice",
     "items": [
      "**Para sa ákin** (for me) but **para kay Mary** (for Mary): pronoun → sa, name → kay.",
      "**Áking iná**, **kanyáng amá**: the pronoun takes the ligature **-g** (áki**ng**, kanyá**ng**) before a noun.",
      "The book's examples also put sa before nouns: **para sa mga batà**, **sa gurò**.",
      "The book writes **kanyá** here; Lesson 8 wrote **kaniyá**. They are the same word."
     ]
